engine: the web build downloads from a server's fast-download URL through the page

The native downloader speaks HTTP over raw sockets, which a browser has not
got, so every sv_downloadurl fetch failed silently in the web build and a
map the browser lacked was the end of a join. net_http_web.c keeps the same
seven entry points and the same completion path (the file lands in
downloaded/<path>, CL_ProcessFile is told, a failed fetch falls back to the
in-band dlfile as natively) but the transfer is the page's: three functions
on Module.http — fetch, poll, take — do it with the browser's fetch, and the
page decides the URL (a cross-origin site goes through the relay's proxy)
and keeps what it fetched.

diff -urN a/engine/common/http/net_http_web.c b/engine/common/http/net_http_web.c
--- a/engine/common/http/net_http_web.c	1969-12-31 17:00:00.000000000 -0700
+++ b/engine/common/http/net_http_web.c	2026-09-14 15:03:22.110433625 -0600
@@ -0,0 +1,282 @@
+/*
+net_http_web.c - the HTTP downloader for the web build: the browser's fetch, not sockets
+Copyright (C) 2026 cs16-web
+
